    "final_answer": "Based on my knowledge, fog horns typically operate at a frequency of approximately **100 Hz** (hertz), though they can range from about 80-200 Hz. \n\nThis low frequency is specifically chosen because:\n- Low-frequency sounds travel much farther through air and water than high frequencies\n- The sound waves can diffract around obstacles like land masses and buildings\n- Fog and other atmospheric conditions don't absorb low frequencies as quickly\n\nThe classic fog horn sound is often described as a deep, resonant \"wooo-woo\" sound that can be heard for many miles in foggy conditions."
  },
